  "appeal_decision": null,
  "description": "I am writing to submit a Non-Material Amendment (NMA) and Listed Building Consent (LBC) application in respect of new timber entrance gates at the above address.\n\nWe propose to install a set of handcrafted timber gates, in keeping with the character of the property and the requirements of both Barnet Council and the Hampstead Garden Suburb Trust. The gates will be 1300 mm high (excluding posts), rising to 1550 mm at the top of the posts, and incorporate underground automated opening mechanisms, as indicated.\n\n\nThe Non-Material Amendment is being submitted in relation to any existing planning permission and involves only a minor design modification.\nThe Listed Building Consent is required due to the Grade II-listed status of the property.\nAshley Niman has advised that both applications should be submitted formally via the Planning Portal and may be dealt with in parallel. They also requested that I mention them in this cover letter.",
